  "question": "Let $A$ be non-singular $3\\times3$ matrix. If $|A|=4$, find $|A^{-1}+\\text{adj}(A)|$.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "First, recall $A^{-1} = \\frac{1}{|A|}\\text{adj}(A)$<br />So, $A^{-1} + \\text{adj}(A) = \\frac{1}{4}\\text{adj}(A)+\\text{adj}(A) = \\frac{5}{4}\\text{adj}(A)$<br /><br />The determinant:<br />$|A^{-1}+\\text{adj}(A)| = |\\frac{5}{4}\\text{adj}(A)| = \\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)^3|\\text{adj}(A)|$ (since $3 \\times 3$ matrix)<br /><br />$|\\text{adj}(A)| = |A|^{2} = 16$<br /><br />So, $|A^{-1}+\\text{adj}(A)| = \\left(\\frac{125}{64}\\right)\\times 16 = \\frac{125}{4}$.",
